job_description:
This local IT support role assists China HQ in rolling out global IT standards. You will deliver day-to-day IT support, equipment maintenance, basic network support and asset register management for office and retail stores.

**Key Responsibilities**

* Assist in implementing corporate IT standards, policies and security controls; support project execution, data collection and corrective action implementation;
* Support IT infrastructure deployment for offices and retail sites, including site survey, hardware racking, cable management and basic system initialisation;
* Perform standardised PC deployment, software installation, routine maintenance and endpoint troubleshooting;
* Conduct regular inspection and maintenance for AV systems, access control, CCTV, IP phones and multi-function printers;
* Support administration of DNS and DHCP services; troubleshoot common network issues on user endpoints;
* Support full lifecycle IT asset management: maintain inventory records, goods receipt, stocktaking, maintenance follow-up and asset retirement documentation;
* Assist with daily monitoring, user permission administration support and routine checks on AD, email, NAS, virtualisation and PBX systems;
* Support HQ security and network teams with on-site activities; assist in communication with local regulators, external auditors and third-party vendors, and report on-site status and issues in a timely manner;
* Maintain operational logs, technical documents and SOPs to implement standardised local IT procedures

**Requirements**

* Proactive and execution-oriented; follow defined procedures for daily IT tasks and report identified issues promptly;

* Able to prioritise daily support tickets; escalate unresolved issues in a timely manner to achieve proper closure;
* Practical knowledge of PC hardware, Windows OS and macOS, common office software; experience with OS reinstallation and endpoint troubleshooting;
* Basic understanding of TCP/IP, DHCP, DNS and capable of resolving typical office network faults;
* Hands-on IT skills to complete equipment installation and maintenance following standard operating procedures;
* Basic awareness of Windows Server, Active Directory, email, NAS and virtualisation; relevant working experience is a plus;
* Fluent in Arabic and English. Able to collaborate in a multicultural environment

**Please note: Please note that only candidates selected for further consideration will receive a response.**

